	"notes": "Svelte's docs use the same three-column shape as Wikipedia and Kubernetes — links on the left, the article in the middle, an on-this-page list on the right — but with its own twist: the two side columns are flexible tracks, yet the actual link lists inside them are a fixed width and simply slide closer to the middle column as the window narrows, or drift outward as it widens, so a huge monitor just adds blank space at the far edges instead of making anything bigger. The middle column itself does grow, but only up to about 760px, then stops. Below about 768px, all three columns disappear and are replaced by a five-icon bar fixed to the BOTTOM of the screen — an unusual choice, since the same promotional banner sits at the TOP of the page on a phone but moves to a fixed bar at the bottom of the screen on a desktop, something only a picture at both sizes would show you.",
